<p>Dates use the proleptic Gregorian calendar for four-digit years <strong>0000–9999</strong>, including year zero; a leap year is divisible by 4 except centuries not divisible by 400. Date values MUST be strings and real dates. Quoting dates is recommended, not a validity condition when YAML core already produces a string. No host-language year-0–99 substitution is allowed. Staleness uses whole UTC calendar days and an explicit <code>today</code> date; future dates are valid and not stale.</p>
<p>The filename rule applies in every directory and every input path. A CLI MAY offer an explicitly named draft mode that skips only filename matching and reports that it did so. Canonical <code>validate</code>, sharing and rendering do not inherit such an exemption from a directory name. A draft can also use the filename <code>HUMANS.md</code>.</p>
<p>New-profile compilers SHOULD propose explicit <code>visibility: private</code>. They MUST preserve an existing profile’s effective visibility, including omitted <code>org</code>, unless the owner explicitly approves a scope change. Omission is not a migration to private and must not be introduced into an existing private profile.</p>
