<h3 id="35-interrupting-when-to-interrupt-me">3.5 <code>interrupting</code>: when to interrupt me</h3>
<div class="table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Table: 3.5 interrupting: when to interrupt me"><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Field</th>
<th>Values</th>
<th>Meaning</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>interrupt_for</code></td>
<td><code>blocking_only</code>, <code>blocking_or_risky</code>, <code>anything</code></td>
<td>What justifies stopping to ask</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>group_by</code></td>
<td><code>project</code>, <code>none</code></td>
<td>How several pending messages are grouped</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>when_focused</code></td>
<td><code>summary_later</code>, <code>urgent_only</code>, <code>as_usual</code></td>
<td>Reserved focus preference; stored but inactive in this draft</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>channel_hint</code></td>
<td><code>async_written</code>, <code>sync_call</code>, <code>either</code></td>
<td>Preferred channel for complex topics</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>progress_updates</code></td>
<td><code>every_message</code>, <code>phase_changes</code>, <code>end_only</code></td>
<td>How a long task reports where it stands: in every message (“step 3 of 5”), only when a phase starts or ends, or once at the end</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>quiet_hours</code></td>
<td>mapping: <code>time_zone</code>, <code>from</code>, <code>to</code>, optional <code>all_day</code></td>
